# Simulated tool setter — LCNC Suite sim configs only (a real machine has a
# real probe and never loads this). Sourced by core_sim_{3,5,6}.hal in place
# of their `net probe-in => motion.probe-input`; each of them then fixes the
# PLATE with `setp sim-toolsetter.0.plate-x/-y/-z` — the tool setter is a
# physical fixture of the profile, not the WebUI's setting (Codex R44 ST-I01).
#
# motion.probe-input = the WebUI's manual trip (signal probe-in, "Simulate
# probe trip") OR the tool tip reaching the plate. sim_toolsetter compares in
# the servo thread: the control point (the JOINT positions 0..2, joint.N.pos-fb
# — never the motor positions, which carry the home / motor offset: Codex R44
# ST-I02) inside the plate's X/Y window, and its Z minus the spindle tool's
# TABLE length at or below the plate surface. sim_toolsetter_feed.py supplies
# the table length — the sim's physical tool length, so a measurement with the
# WebUI's tool setter set to this plate returns it.
#
# The component is built by install.sh (`sudo halcompile --install
# sim_toolsetter/sim_toolsetter.comp`); without it LinuxCNC refuses this file
# ("module not found") and scripts/config_sync_check.py names the command.

loadrt sim_toolsetter
addf sim-toolsetter.0 servo-thread
setp sim-toolsetter.0.radius 25

loadusr -Wn sim-toolsetter-feed python3 sim_toolsetter/sim_toolsetter_feed.py

net sim-ts-x        joint.0.pos-fb                  => sim-toolsetter.0.x
net sim-ts-y        joint.1.pos-fb                  => sim-toolsetter.0.y
net sim-ts-z        joint.2.pos-fb                  => sim-toolsetter.0.z
net sim-ts-length   sim-toolsetter-feed.tool-length => sim-toolsetter.0.tool-length
net sim-ts-enable   sim-toolsetter-feed.enable      => sim-toolsetter.0.enable

net probe-in => sim-toolsetter.0.manual
net probe-input sim-toolsetter.0.out => motion.probe-input
